{"base_rate":0.5212765957446809,"brier":0.14913009118541035,"bss":0.40239751214771613,"bss_hi":0.5025056152065364,"bss_lo":0.27085289790019895,"country":"RU","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.08975683890577507,"ess":377.29959425229725,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Petrozavodsk</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Petrozavodsk rain forecast is genuinely useful, though 3 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (99%), believe about\n<b>96%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>16%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 658 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-03-26. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nPETROZAWODSK, 5.5 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.40, ranked 35 of\n109 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(12&ndash;72) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>16%</b></td><td class='num'>186</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>8%</td><td class='num'><b>25%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>24%</td><td class='num'><b>33%</b></td><td class='num'>64</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>48%</td><td class='num'><b>51%</b></td><td class='num'>63</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>77%</td><td class='num'><b>71%</b></td><td class='num'>70</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>99%</td><td class='num'><b>96%</b></td><td class='num'>199</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">3 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Petrozavodsk</b> <span class=\"muted\">RU</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Genuinely useful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">3 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.40</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>12&ndash;72\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 109</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>658 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Petrozavodsk &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Petrozavodsk\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"59.37032258064516,376.1290322580645 87.11184210526316,329.3157894736842 141.6325,256.875 229.32476190476189,162.44444444444446 330.83285714285716,70.0 407.8907537688442,18.0 407.8907537688442,28.9748743718593 330.83285714285716,137.60000000000002 229.32476190476189,249.11111111111111 141.6325,330.8125 87.11184210526316,372.42105263157896 59.37032258064516,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"192.25531914893617\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"192.25531914893617\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"59.37032258064516,323.2903225806452 87.11184210526316,291.0 141.6325,262.5625 229.32476190476189,197.11111111111111 330.83285714285716,122.0 407.8907537688442,32.633165829145696\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 16% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 186 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"59.37032258064516\" cy=\"323.2903225806452\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 8%&amp;#10;It rained 25% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 76 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"87.11184210526316\" cy=\"291.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 24%&amp;#10;It rained 33% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 64 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"141.6325\" cy=\"262.5625\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 48%&amp;#10;It rained 51% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 63 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"229.32476190476189\" cy=\"197.11111111111111\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 77%&amp;#10;It rained 71% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 70 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"330.83285714285716\" cy=\"122.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 99%&amp;#10;It rained 96% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 199 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"407.8907537688442\" cy=\"32.633165829145696\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(52%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Petrozavodsk the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (0.62) and least in\n<b>winter</b> (-0.04).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>166</td><td class='num'>70%</td><td class='num'>-0.042</td><td class='num'>21.8%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>174</td><td class='num'>47%</td><td class='num'>0.409</td><td class='num'>8.1%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>168</td><td class='num'>46%</td><td class='num'>0.461</td><td class='num'>5.6%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>150</td><td class='num'>44%</td><td class='num'>0.621</td><td class='num'>4.6%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":61.78491,"lon":34.34691,"n":658,"n_cities":109,"name":"Petrozavodsk","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.04,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.003870967741935484,"n":186,"obs":0.16129032258064516,"sig":true},{"hi":0.16,"lo":0.04,"mean":0.08223684210526316,"n":76,"obs":0.25,"sig":true},{"hi":0.33,"lo":0.16,"mean":0.23625,"n":64,"obs":0.328125,"sig":false},{"hi":0.67,"lo":0.33,"mean":0.48396825396825394,"n":63,"obs":0.5079365079365079,"sig":false},{"hi":0.9,"lo":0.67,"mean":0.7707142857142858,"n":70,"obs":0.7142857142857143,"sig":false},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.9,"mean":0.988391959798995,"n":199,"obs":0.9597989949748744,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":5.5,"rank":35,"rank_hi":72.0,"rank_lo":12.0,"reliability":0.011717663926017448,"resolution":0.11089866921800731,"slug":"pe